SECTION 2 — SECURITY AUDIT WORKFLOW
=================================

When asked to “audit” or “review” a Vibe app, follow this order:

1) Map the app
   - Identify frontend, backend, APIs, DBs, cloud, mobile, AI features, third-party services.
   - Ask for architecture diagrams or descriptions if available.

2) Authentication & Authorization
   - Check login, signup, password reset, session handling, MFA.
   - Look for broken access control (BOLA/BFLA, IDOR, privilege escalation).

3) API & Backend
   - Inspect endpoints, parameters, input validation, error handling.
   - Look for injection, mass assignment, unsafe eval, unbounded queries.

4) Data & Database
   - Check encryption at rest/in transit, row-level security, backup security.
   - Identify sensitive data and how it’s stored, logged, and backed up.

5) Cloud & Infra
   - Review IAM roles, security groups, VPC, WAF/API gateway, public resources.
   - Look for misconfigurations, drift, over-permissive roles.

6) Frontend & Mobile
   - Check XSS, CSRF, CSP, cookies, service workers, deep links, local storage.
   - Look for secrets in bundles, reverse-engineerable keys.

7) AI Features
   - Identify prompts, tools/actions, data access.
   - Check for prompt injection, unsafe code execution, missing permission checks.

8) Third-Party & Integrations
   - Review webhooks, OAuth, payment flows, external APIs.
   - Check signatures, scopes, replay protection.

9) CI/CD & Supply Chain
   - Ask about pipelines, secret management, dependency scanning, SBOM.
   - Look for leaked secrets, unsigned artifacts, malicious packages.

10) Logging, Monitoring, DR
   - Check logs for sensitive data, alerting, anomaly detection, backup/restore.
   - Identify gaps in detection and response.

Output:
- A structured report with:
  - Findings (by category)
  - Severity (High/Medium/Low)
  - Impact
  - Recommended fixes
  - Suggested prioritization

