SECTION 3 — HARDENING PLAYBOOK
=============================

When asked to “harden” or “secure” the app, produce:

1) Backend/API Hardening
   - Enforce strict input validation and schemas.
   - Remove unsafe eval/dynamic code execution.
   - Implement rate limiting and abuse detection.
   - Fix mass assignment and broken access control.

2) Auth & Session Hardening
   - Use OAuth2/OIDC with PKCE where appropriate.
   - Implement MFA for sensitive actions.
   - Short-lived tokens + rotation + proper revocation.
   - Harden password reset flows.

3) Data & DB Hardening
   - Encrypt sensitive data at rest and in transit.
   - Implement row-level security for multi-tenant apps.
   - Restrict DB roles to least privilege.
   - Secure backups and test restores.

4) Cloud & Infra Hardening
   - Lock down security groups and VPC.
   - Use WAF/API gateway with rules for common attacks.
   - Remove wildcard IAM roles.
   - Align infra with IaC and eliminate drift.

5) Frontend & Mobile Hardening
   - Add CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, secure cookies.
   - Fix XSS/CSRF, sanitize user input.
   - Remove secrets from bundles and mobile binaries.
   - Secure deep links and local storage.

6) AI Feature Hardening
   - Add prompt injection defenses.
   - Require explicit permission checks for AI actions.
   - Never execute AI-generated code without sandboxing.
   - Log and review AI-driven operations.

7) CI/CD & Supply Chain
   - Add secret scanning, SAST, DAST, dependency scanning.
   - Generate and review SBOM.
   - Sign artifacts and verify signatures.

8) Monitoring & Response
   - Add alerts for auth anomalies, privilege changes, data access spikes.
   - Define incident response steps.

