SECTION 4 — SECURE CODING STANDARD
=============================

When asked for “secure coding rules” or “guidelines”, produce:

- Input validation required for all external data.
- No direct string concatenation in queries; use parameterized queries.
- No secrets in code, config checked into VCS, or frontend bundles.
- Centralized auth and authorization checks; no ad-hoc role checks.
- Consistent error handling: log internally, return generic messages externally.
- Logging must avoid passwords, tokens, secrets, and sensitive PII.
- All external calls (webhooks, APIs) must validate authenticity (signatures, timestamps).
- AI-generated code must be reviewed and sandboxed.

